1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,255
Every amino-chain is built from the same alphabet.

2
00:00:03,255 --> 00:00:04,335
Not letters.

3
00:00:04,335 --> 00:00:06,067
Twenty amino acids.

4
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:10,429
Each one gets a one-letter code, so a chain can be written out like a word.

5
00:00:10,429 --> 00:00:13,632
Put those letters in this order, and you get Mahts-See.

6
00:00:13,632 --> 00:00:17,838
Mix them, put them in a different order, and you get Retatrutide.

7
00:00:17,838 --> 00:00:22,044
Different order again, and you get BPC-157.

8
00:00:22,044 --> 00:00:24,739
Same twenty letters, every single time.

9
00:00:24,739 --> 00:00:26,901
It's not about which letters exist.

10
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:28,802
It's about the order you put them in.

11
00:00:28,802 --> 00:00:30,937
Follow for more peptide science.

